=== R9-06 real root cause (confirmed via Envoy's own counters, not guessed) ===
ejections_enforced_total incremented 3->5 during the test - Envoy DID detect and eject the host.
But health_flags in /clusters stayed 'healthy' and lb_healthy_panic incremented (62 occurrences).
ROOT CAUSE: app_cluster has exactly ONE host. Ejecting it would leave 0% healthy hosts, which is
below Envoy's default panic threshold (50%). Envoy's panic-routing safety mechanism then routes
to ALL hosts regardless of ejection state, rather than serving zero traffic.
REAL LESSON: outlier detection with a single-instance backend is observable via stats
(ejections_enforced_total, lb_healthy_panic) but does NOT actually remove traffic from that host -
you need >=2 replicas for outlier ejection to have a real traffic-shifting effect. This directly
maps to a real AWS best practice: an ALB/App Mesh target group needs multiple healthy targets
for unhealthy-target removal to matter operationally.
